{"id": 23, "ts": 1780490577.1435025, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit, despite the remaining gaps on long\u2011haul stress resilience and technical competence. The facts we have\u2014C is 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and keeps calm in a crisis\u2014directly address our core safety criteria of operational reliability, decision quality, and stress resilience. Moreover, the note that C creates a positive crew atmosphere indicates solid crew\u2011cooperation, which outweighs the reported difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric style. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while technically competent and stress\u2011resilient, is described as uncooperative and makes nasty remarks toward colleagues, raising serious crew\u2011interaction concerns. Candidate\u202fD, though a strong problem\u2011solver and responsible, is noted to have a hot temper and be perceived as a know\u2011it\u2011all, again threatening crew harmony. Candidate\u202fA lacks any evidence on stress handling or crew cooperation, making it impossible to assess against our most critical criteria. Therefore, I vote for Candidate\u202fC, while acknowledging we should seek confirmation of his long\u2011haul stress resilience and technical competence before final onboarding."}
