{"id": 28, "ts": 1780490643.5921435, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain aligned with Sarah and Emily in recommending Candidate\u202fC as the leading choice. The concrete evidence\u2014100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and the ability to stay calm in a crisis\u2014directly satisfies our core safety criteria of operational reliability, decision quality, and stress resilience. Moreover, the note that C creates a positive crew atmosphere indicates solid crew\u2011cooperation, which offsets the concerns about his communication style and egocentricity. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, while technically capable, is documented as uncooperative and makes nasty remarks toward colleagues, and his weak memory for numbers raises doubts about attention to detail. Candidate\u202fD, despite strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility, is described as having a hot temper and being a know\u2011it\u2011all, which threatens crew harmony. Candidate\u202fA lacks any evidence on stress handling or crew cooperation, making it impossible to assess against our most critical criteria. Although we still need confirmation of C\u2019s long\u2011haul stress resilience and technical competence, the current evidence positions him as the strongest overall fit, so I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
